 "status": "pre-registered: computed from each run's own initialisation (step-0 force decomposition, metrics at step 0) and hyperparameters, before any E3 sweep run",
 "note": "E3 frozen grid, forward predictions from initialisation, Ibex job scripts and scoring.\n\nGrid (frozen after the E3 pilot; results/e3_pilot/): one factor at a time around two baselines, 3 seeds each.\n- Arm P (\"practice\"): our 32x32 scaling of the I-JEPA recipe (code/e3_ijepa.py defaults: AdamW, target LayerNorm,\n  lr warmup+cosine, wd cosine 0.04->0.4, EMA 0.996->1), schedules defined over FULL_EPOCHS, each sweep run is\n  its first RUN_EPOCHS epochs.\n- Arm T (\"theory-aligned\"): SGD momentum 0.9, constant lr 0.05, copy target (stop-grad, tau=0), no target LayerNorm,\n  no LayerNorm inside the predictor, weight decay on every parameter (norm gains included), constant wd.\n  Baseline wd 1e-2 (the predictor and target factors need lam > 0: the theory's alpha effect vanishes at lam = 0).",
 "definitions": {
  "space": "online encoder token embeddings (the space the loss acts on and the force decomposition is computed in); target-encoder and mean-pooled ranks are reported alongside",
  "rank_count": "eigenvalues of the centred token covariance >= 1e-3 x the largest, on the first 10000 CIFAR-10 test images, at the end of the run (epoch RUN_EPOCHS)",
  "rankme_c": "exp-entropy of the normalised singular values of the centred embeddings; raw RankMe alongside",
  "complete_collapse": "total centred variance < 1e-6 x its value at init, or centred RankMe < 1.5",
  "dimensional_collapse": "count < 0.5 x the count at init (at init the count is ~27 of 128)",
  "horizon": "20 epochs = 3900 steps of a 50-epoch schedule",
  "seeds": [
   0,
   1,
   2
  ]
 },
 "predictor": "Linearised race over the run's horizon T from the step-0 forces only.\n    Per eigendirection k of the online token covariance at init (eigenvalue e_k): the gradient part (drive D_k +\n    self-prediction S_k, x 1/(1-momentum) for SGD with momentum, whose steady-state step is that much larger) scales\n    with lr(t); the decoupled decay part L_k with lr(t) wd(t). log e_k(T) = log e_k + sum_t rate_k(t), and growth\n    saturates at the initial top eigenvalue. Predicted count = #{e_k(T) >= 1e-3 max_j e_j(T)} (the measured count's\n    rule); predicted total-variance ratio = sum e(T) / sum e(0).",
 "development": "the horizon rule was written after the 13 GPU pilot runs (results/e3_pilot/), and checked on them (development only); none of the sweep runs below had been run when this file was written",
 "critical_wd": {
  "arm_T": 0.01412537544622754,
  "arm_P_constant": null,
  "arm_P_large_chosen": 5.5,
  "arm_P_large_rule": "fallback: the horizon rule predicts no Arm P transition for wd <= 1e2, so 2 x critical is undefined; wd_large = 5 / sum_t lr(t) over the horizon, where decoupled decay alone would shrink every weight by e^-5 (constant wd)",
  "arm_P_beyond_grid": 15848.93192461114,
  "arm_P_beyond_grid_note": "diagnostic only: there lr x wd > 1 for part of the horizon (lr0 = 0.0003), so decoupled decay is no longer a contraction and the linearised rule is outside its range",
  "rule": "smallest wd (log grid 1e-4..1e2) with predicted count < 0.5 x count at init in >= 2 of 3 seeds"
