  "C-dir (forward)": "for each factor, each adjacent pair of grid values (each mask setting against the base) whose predicted mean counts differ by more than the tolerance max(2, sd_a + sd_b) (sd = sample standard deviation of the predicted count over the 3 seeds) has a predicted sign; the measured centred RankMe change has that sign in >= 2 of 3 seeds (plan default). Every other pair is registered as an explicit null ('no predicted difference'), which holds if the measured mean counts differ by at most max(2, sd_a + sd_b) of the measured counts. Scored as the fractions of signed pairs and of nulls that hold, and listed",
  "C-loc wd (forward)": "location of the dimensional-collapse transition in weight decay (Arm T wd sweep): the observed transition (geometric midpoint of the last healthy and first collapsed grid value; collapsed = online count < 0.5 x its value at init in >= 2 of 3 seeds) lies within a factor of 2 of the predicted critical wd (plan default for log-scaled knobs)",
  "C-theory signs (forward)": "signs from theory/derivations.md Sec. 4 independent of the init forces: rank falls with weight decay (both arms), with the predictor lr multiplier (both arms, lam > 0) and with predictor depth (Arm P); nosg ends in complete collapse (total online variance < 1e-6 x init, or centred RankMe < 1.5; Prop. 5); frozen target at standard init does not collapse (online count >= 0.5 x init; Sec. 4 frozen row with c|w0| > lam); EMA rate changes the count by less than the seed spread at matched schedule (EMA changes time scales, not the threshold) - each scored per seed majority",
